  "metadata": {
    "audit_timestamp": "2026-11-19T09:36:00.005468+00:00",
    "milestone": "Milestone 15.1",
    "audit_title": "Independent Evaluation Audit & Supervised POI Matcher Technical Validation",
    "formal_verdict": "AUDIT_PASSED_WITH_CORRECTIONS",
    "executive_verdict_rationale": "The core training and spatial-component isolation guarantees are mathematically verified: 0 cross-split connected components, 0 shared OSM nodes, 0 shared Overture nodes, and 100% feature completeness. However, the reported F1 = 1.0000 on the held-out test set is an artifact of high benchmark bimodality and small sample size (N=18, of which 13 come from Dataset C). Furthermore, the error analysis erroneously reported '0 errors across 100 annotated pairs' by omitting the 8 ambiguous cases (all 8 of which were predicted NON_MATCH by the model). In universe inference, while ~6,200 additional matches are genuine recoveries where Rule V1's guardrails were overly conservative, the model generates ~256 false-positive matches on ATM vs Bank Branch pairs due to brand-level over-matching. With these reporting corrections, explicit provenance disaggregation, and exact TreeSHAP attribution implemented, the system passes audit under AUDIT_PASSED_WITH_CORRECTIONS."
  },
